- Story & Context: While sequestered in the damp cabin of an impounded cargo vessel anchored off Apapa, bassist Dele Lawson conceived this confessional rhythm after monitoring twenty-four continuous hours of VHF maritime distress signals during a blinding Harmattan dust-fog. The cabin reeked of diesel fumes, damp burlap, and rusted iron while Dele nursed the fresh grief of an abandoned romance in Manchester, meticulously tuning his rubbery bassline to mirror the off-beat, mournful groans of tugboats lost in the red-white haze. In a single uncut tape pass, he slowed the multitrack speed by twenty percent while the band laid down gossamer synth strings, framing Mhairi’s heartbreak in a breathy sigh: "You answered two nautical miles too late."
