- Story & Context: Dock folklore along the Mersey holds that when coastal advection fog turned dense enough to swallow harbor radar, this track’s chorus-drenched synth strings and answering baritone horn lines bled across coastal shortwave radio, serving as a phantom navigation beacon for disoriented mariners. The myth crystallized when a Danish bulk freighter drifted clear of the treacherous Formby sandbanks because the helmsman mistook the track's dual-saxophone call-and-response for the acoustic buoy of the lightship. When the fog finally broke at sunrise to reveal an emerald optical flash on the sea horizon, the band captured the tape machine's lingering spring-reverb feedback underneath a fading falsetto vow: "Look for the emerald flare across the gray."
